    "description": "Unique neocom-back collection for every HTTP endpoint currently served by the Nest app, aligned with OpenAPI under tools/openapi/ and ExceptionCatalog outcomes.\n\n**Specs covered**\n- `pilot-service-v0.1.0.yaml` \u2014 GET /v1/pilots/{pilotId}\n- `industry-service-v0.1.0.yaml` \u2014 GET /v1/pilots/{pilotId}/blueprints\n- Auth \u2014 POST /v1/auth/callback + TOKEN_UNAVAILABLE via access-cookie middleware\n- **OAuth2 \u2014 EVE SSO (real ESI)** \u2014 authorize URL, code exchange, cookie session, authenticated calls\n\n**Not included:** `gateway-adapter-service-v0.2.0.yaml` (legacy / not a neocom-back route).\n\nError bodies use NeocomError: `{ errors: [{ code, description, field?, container?, value? }], traceId? }`.\n\nUse the **NEOCOM local** environment. For real ESI: run the OAuth2 folder (or bind an existing tokens.json character).",
